The repo is scaffolded. Here's what's in it:

```
deckagent/
├── SPEC.md             # Full architecture spec
├── AGENTS.md            # Build instructions for Devin
├── README.md            # Public-facing description
├── packages/
│   ├── cloudflare-worker/   # CF Worker (MCP endpoint + OAuth + tunnel)
│   ├── desktop-daemon/      # System tray daemon
│   ├── mcp-server/         # Shared MCP tool definitions
│   └── cli/                # Installer CLI
└── reference/
    └── desktop-commander/   # Cloned for reference (MIT)
```

The first commit has the spec + structure. Let me push it.

The full spec covers why it exists, architecture decisions (CF Worker vs relay, WebSocket tunnel, OAuth), detailed data flow, complete tool list (18 tools in v1, 8 tools in v2), security model (policy engine, device tokens, OAuth), build order (4 phases), and a direct Devin prompt to get started.

Everything you need to hand this to Devin. Want me to push the commit, or do you want to review the spec first?
